    "turn_text": "try that and frequently the people run, frequently the ringleaders are the ones that run into the night. And it's very difficult to track them down. You know, in addition to the wall, we need a road. When I went down to the Tucson area, when I think of a desert, I think of sand and cactuses, but that desert is really rocks. So even if you try to drive vehicle over there, you'd be going maybe two or three miles an hour. I mean, it's really difficult. So that's another thing that we need there and why so many people get away.",
