    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "Well, they feel they're handling it right now. I mean, it's difficult, but even during the rush, they felt they looked at everybody and sent somebody for more help. Now, they make a big deal of somebody dies, but you got to remember the volume of people coming across. When you have 150,000 people in one month, a lot of them coming from areas that are not well off or walking in here, they really feel they did at that point. I think they're probably more since then. But at that point, when I was there, they said three people had passed away. They thought they were really doing a good job given the population they had to deal with.",
