  {
    "episode_id": 90825,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90825.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "Well, President Trump tried to restrict this asylum treatment, where all you have to do is say, I'm in danger if I return home. He tried to restrict it to people who are really coming here for asylum, and not just because America is a wealthier country. And common sense will tell you, let's say we're in Shabweig in Wisconsin right now. If you feel threatened in Shabweig in Wisconsin because of a gang or something, where are you going to go? You're not going to go to Honduras, right? You're going to go maybe to Manitowoc or maybe to Fond du Lac. Maybe if you're really in danger, go to Illinois. So we have to clarify the asylum laws. You do not get asylum here unless you're from a country next door, Mexico or Canada or something. We're not going to have the whole world come here. And by the way, the whole world is coming here. As far as customs, which gets a small fraction of the people at border patrol gets, they told us we were down there in the Laredo sector anyway. There are big three countries where Venezuela, Cuba and Congo, which indicates the word is out worldwide that you can come into the United States right now.",
