        "text": "Asylum should be granted only to individuals from neighboring countries like Mexico or Canada.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "People facing threats in places like Shabweig, Wisconsin, would likely seek refuge in nearby U.S. cities rather than returning to their home countries.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The current asylum system allows people from around the world to enter the U.S., creating a perception that anyone can come regardless of origin.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Customs officials in the Laredo sector reported that many asylum seekers are arriving from Venezuela, Cuba, and the Democratic Republic of Congo.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "There is widespread global awareness that the U.S. currently has open asylum policies.",
