    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "Well, we finally got a few new judges down there, so we wouldn't have to wait in three years, nowhere near as many judges as we wanted. A frustrating thing is, while I get along with individual Democrats, the Democrat leadership clearly wants to do nothing. And whether he's now finally has some money that he won in court, for a wall. The wall will be helpful, but remember, most people just turn them into the asylum rules anyway. Nevertheless, the wall will send a message we're serious about our laws and will prevent some people from coming across. I want to digress. I'm going to wait and see what type of wall it is, too. Talking to the border patrol, right now the wall, and there's a lot of wall down there. The wall being built, was built by President Bush, President Clinton, some under President Obama, perhaps replaced, is 16 to 18 feet high. The Border Patrol wants a 30 feet high. It won't keep out everything, but it's a deterrent to try to get over 30 feet. And furthermore, it takes time, which gives the Border Patrol a chance to get over there. So that's one thing he's had success on. He hasn't had as much success on the asylum as we'd like him to have. But, like I said, and the other thing we've got to deal with is birthright citizenship. The last time it was down there, and for some reason it didn't click, but I had a staff down there and clicked with him, a very high percentage of the women who you see being processed are pregnant. So that's what you hear, you know, that some women's four or five months pregnant, maybe it's time to take a walk north. So my baby can be born an American citizen. Or we also hear, you know, Chinese in particular flying into San Diego, flying into California. having a baby here. That's not the way to pick. future American citizens. I believe that of the 40 wealthiest countries in the world, or at least the sizable 40 of wealthiest countries in the world, the United States is one of only two countries that has what we call birthright citizenship. Just show up here, have a baby. It's an American citizen. Of course, once that child's American citizen, easier for the parents to stay there to take care of that person, eligible for all sorts of government benefits, that sort of thing.",
